  "answer": "I found no past ticket that reports this exact problem. In your case the taskbar is auto-hidden and showing, and the Shortcut Guide indicators are drawn on top of the taskbar items instead of over the matching icons. Nearby tickets describe different problems. PowerToys#291 is about the old Shortcut Guide showing no numbers when the taskbar auto-hides, and it was closed after v2 shipped in 0.100. PowerToys#48435 is about indicators glitching when the taskbar is not at the bottom. PowerToys#38192 asks for Shortcut Guide to bring up a hidden taskbar. Please keep this ticket open as a new bug. Include your Windows version, the display scaling, and the taskbar position. Also say whether the overlay is still misplaced when the taskbar is set to always show."
 },
